  "result": {
    "summary": "A crushing English victory against odds of perhaps three or four to one. The French lost roughly 6,000-10,000 men, including the Constable, three dukes and a great part of the nobility, with Orléans, Bourbon and Boucicaut taken prisoner; English losses were a few hundred (records name at least 112), among them Edward of York and the Earl of Suffolk.",
    "casualties": {
      "A": "~112 named dead, perhaps 500-600 in all (York, Suffolk, Dafydd Gam)",
      "B": "~6,000-10,000 killed (Constable d'Albret, Alençon, Bar, Brabant); 700-2,200 captured"
    }
  },
